atus="new"><text>See also references of EP     1115213A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HITACHI LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HITACHI, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWABATA ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGUMA KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TASHIRO KOREHUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE DAI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWABATA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGUMA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TASHIRO, KOREHUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, DAI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A train detecting method highly resistant to noise for detecting a train according to presence/absence of demodulation because of decrease of the level of the received signal due to axel short circuit so as to make a train detection by using a frequency-modulated train detecting signal, wherein before the frequency-dependent demodulation a gain processing for amplifying the amplitude of the signal, a limiter processing for restricting the amplitude of the output signal of the gain processing to a certain level, and a filter processing for eliminating harmonics produced because of the limiter processing are combinedly performed to arbitrarily set the lower limit of the level of the demodulatable signal by means of the gain, thus arbitrarily setting the threshold of train detection.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de détection de train hautement résistant au bruit, conçu pour détecter un train en fonction de la présence/absence de démodulation du fait de la diminution de l'intensité du signal reçu consécutivement à un court-circuit, au moyen d'un signal de détection de train, modulé en fréquence. Avant la démodulation dépendant de la fréquence, un traitement du gain pour l'amplification de l'amplitude du signal, un traitement de limitation pour la restriction de l'amplitude du signal de sortie du traitement de gain à un certain niveau, et un traitement de filtrage pour l'élimination des harmoniques produits par le traitement de limitation, sont assurés conjointement de sorte que la limite inférieure de l'intensité du signal démodulable soit fixée au moyen du gain, et donc que le seuil de détection de train soit fixé arbitraitement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>